      "value": "@{5b776a5b417f6727e8e87b67|full_name}: I actually just now did a bit of testing because I had a hunch. Turns out it is indeed the exact same issue as the canny I linked. The reason it happens in stations is because VRChat is trying to override your seated animator with the Station's supplied one. The problem is most people do not set an animator in their station, so it overrides the default without supplying a new one.\nI confirmed this by going to an MMD dance world and tried doing gestures/state changes while in the dance station. It worked 100% perfectly there.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
